Q: Looping through array and pass data to function A: <p>Maybe using collections</p>

<pre><code>return collect($this-&gt;getTickets($uid))-&gt;map(function($ticket){

    return [$ticket, $this-&gt;getTicket($ticket['id'])];

})-&gt;flatten(1);
</code></pre>

Q: How to make multiple functions in foreach with id? A: <p>I'm not sure whether this would achieve what you want to <em>happen</em>, but you can create multiple functions in a loop by using anonymous functions:</p>

<pre><code>$functions = [];
foreach ($posts as $post) {
    $seusag = $post['uagent'];
    $functions[$post] = function () use ($seusag) {
        return $seusag;
    }
}
</code></pre>

<p>I don't know whether <code>$seusag</code> inside the function will remain the same, though; I don't think it will.</p>

Q: Issue with data retrieving A: <p>i recommend u to use active record like this:</p>

<pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;select('*');
$this-&gt;db-&gt;from('orders'); 
$this-&gt;db-&gt;join('client', 'client.client_email = orders.email'); 
$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get();
</code></pre>

